  {
    "slide": 25,
    "name": "TextBox 16",
    "text": "Think of the search like walking over hills. Today’s method only walks uphill. That is fast and safe, but you can get stuck on a steep part of the hill when a better peak is nearby.\r\rSimulated annealing sometimes takes a downhill step early, so you can leave a trap and reach a better overall schedule. As the search “cools,” those downhill steps become rare, and we settle on the best plan we found.",
